~ start
if first == true:
	=>< Introduction
	set first = false
else:
	=>< Reintroduction
if check_feathers():
	What will you do?
	- Forgiving yourself is the first step to freeing yourself. (Give)
		=>< Give_Dialogue
		do give_feathers()
		do save_npc()
		do disappear()
		=> END
	- This is all your fault. You don’t deserve the feathers you hold. (Take)
		=>< Take_Dialogue
		do take_feathers()
		do doom_player()
		do disappear()
		=> END
	- ... (Ignore)
		=> END
else:
	What will you do?
	- ??? [if check_feathers()]
		=>< Give_Dialogue
		do give_feathers()
		do disappear()
		=> END
	- This is all your fault. You don’t deserve the feathers you hold. (Take)
		=>< Take_Dialogue
		do take_feathers()
		do disappear()
		=> END
	- ... (Ignore)
		=> END

~ Introduction
The Thief: …I can’t do it. I can’t hold them any longer.
The Thief: I took them. The feathers, I mean. I just needed to escape, to get out of here, so I took as many as I could carry…
The Thief: But I can’t bear the weight any longer. The looks on their faces, the guilt; it’s so heavy…
The Thief: They wouldn’t forgive me. I wouldn’t forgive me. I don’t deserve it.

 => END

~ Reintroduction
The Thief: Are you here to condemn me, too?
 => END

~ Give_Dialogue
The Thief: I… you’re giving these to me?
The Thief: Huh, they feel so light…
The Thief: Thank you, I can feel strength returning to my legs. 
The Thief: I’ll repay this kindness someday, I swear it. To you and to them.

 => END

~ Take_Dialogue
The Thief: You’re right…
The Thief: I deserve this prison. I deserve this pain.
The Thief: There’s no reason to hold on any longer.

 => END